          %h3#the__of_order_6
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            of order 6
          %p
            The group of permutations of three letters,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_3
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mi b
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle a,b : a^3, b^2,(a b)^2 \rangle.
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            corresponds to the 3-cycle,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 123
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (123)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            corresponds to any transposition.
          %h3#_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot+group"} Knot groups
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trefoil+knot"} trefoil
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot+group"} knot group
            has two useful presentations:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi a
                        %mn 3
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi b
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle a,b : a^3= b^2\rangle
                , which displays the fact that the trefoil is a (2,3)-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus+knot"}> torus knot
                ; and
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle x,y : x y x = y x y\rangle
                , which shows the link between this group and the Artin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group"} braid group
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Br
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br3
          %h3#_3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coxeter+groups"} Coxeter groups
          %p
            At the entry on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coxeter+groups"} Coxeter groups
            one finds the following:
          %p
            %strong Definition
            A
            %em Coxeter matrix
            over an index
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is a symmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 3
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \colon I \times I \to \{1, 2, 3, \ldots, \infty\}
          %p
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M(i, i) = 1
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M(i, j) \gt 1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_{i,j} = M(i, j)
            %strong Coxeter group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_M
            is the group presented as having generators
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_i
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s_i s_j)^{m_{i, j}} = 1
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i, j \in I
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_{i, j} \neq \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_{i, j}
            is the order of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_i s_j
            (as is easily shown), and these orders determine the group.
          %p We thus have an infinite family of group presentations.
          %h2#discussion Discussion
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em> ‘Relations’ and ‘relators’
                \: In the discussion of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_3
                above we had a
                %strong relation
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mi a
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b a = a^2b
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X)
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong relators
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = 1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                is a word in the generators. In the example
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b a = a^2b
                can be easily shown to imply and be implied by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a b a b = 1
            %li
              %p Given a group presentation as above, we have a short exact sequence,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to N \to F \to G \to 1,
          %p
            where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = F(X)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a subset of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = N(R)
            is the normal closure in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            of the set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            acts on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            by conjugation:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ucu
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi for
                  %mi c
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^u c = ucu^{-1}, for  c\in N, u \in F
            and the elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            are words in the conjugates of the elements of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ε
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi r
                    %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ε
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi …
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ε
                        %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c = {}^{u_1}(r_1^{\varepsilon_1}){}^{u_2}(r_2^{\varepsilon_2})\ldots
                  {}^{u_n}(r_n^{\varepsilon_n})
          %p
            where each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ε
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon_i
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} + 1
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
