                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            which equals 1.
          %h2#transformations_of_a_group_presentation Transformations of a group presentation
          %p
            Given a group presentation, it is natural to perform transformations using substitutions, say adding in one new symbol for a string of generators, and adjusting the presentation accordingly. The valid transformations that do not change the group being presented are formalised as the
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tietze+transformation"} Tietze transformation
          %h2#combinatorial_group_theory Combinatorial group theory
          %p
            The study of group presentations, their transformations etc. forms part of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+group+theory"} combinatorial group theory
          %h2#presentations_of_monoids_and_other_algebraic_and_categorical_structures Presentations of monoids and other algebraic and categorical structures.
          %p
            The theory of group presentations generalises to that of presentations of monoids and then to general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rewriting"} rewriting
            systems.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+presentable+group"} finitely presentable group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+group+theory"} combinatorial group theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrews-Curtis+conjecture"} Andrews-Curtis conjecture
          %h2#references References
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilhelm+Magnus"}> Wilhelm Magnus
                , A. Karras, D. Solitar,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Combinatorial group theory: Presentation of groups in terms of generators and relations
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maa.org/press/maa-reviews/combinatorial-group-theory-presentations-of-groups-in-terms-of-generators-and-relations"} ISBN:0-486-43830-9
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://books.google.com/books?hl=en&lr=&id=1LW4s1RDRHQC&oi=fnd&pg=PP1&ots=WszNa-0hEz&sig=Hn_MTbyLcEreBBNZ8jJtQUVKlZk"} GoogleBooks
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Lawrence+Johnson"}> David Lawrence Johnson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topics in Theory of Group Presentations
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 42
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511629303"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511629303
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Lawrence+Johnson"}> David Lawrence Johnson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Presentations of Groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 15
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139168410"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139168410
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N.+D.+Gilbert"} N. D. Gilbert
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T.+Porter"} T. Porter
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+group+theory"} combinatorial group theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roger+C.+Lyndon"}> Roger C. Lyndon
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+E.+Schupp"} Paul E. Schupp
              = succeed "," do
                %em Combinatorial group theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://elib.tu-darmstadt.de/tocs/94684782.pdf"} toc
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              Derek Holt (notes by Florian Bouyer),
              %em Presentation of Groups
              (2013) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/maths/people/staff/fbouyer/presentation_of_group.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On (finitely) presented groups as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groups"} fundamental groups
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+cell+complex"}> finite
            )
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complexes"} simplicial complexes
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+J.+Rotman"}> Joseph J. Rotman
                , around Thm. 7.34 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An Introduction to Algebraic Topology
                %strong 119
                (1988)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
